x-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":45,\"name\":\"Utah\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/utah-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":46,\"name\":\"Alabama\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/alabama-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":47,\"name\":\"Arkansas\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/arkansas-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":48,\"name\":\"Connecticut\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/connecticut-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":49,\"name\":\"Delaware\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/delaware-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":50,\"name\":\"Hawaii\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/hawaii-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":51,\"name\":\"Iowa\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/iowa-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":52,\"name\":\"Kansas\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/kansas-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":53,\"name\":\"Louisiana\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":54,\"name\":\"Maine\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/maine-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":55,\"name\":\"Montana\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/montana-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":56,\"name\":\"Nebraska\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/nebraska-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":57,\"name\":\"New Mexico\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/new-mexico-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":58,\"name\":\"North Dakota\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/north-dakota-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":59,\"name\":\"Oklahoma\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/oklahoma-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":60,\"name\":\"Rhode Island\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/rhode-island-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":61,\"name\":\"South Carolina\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/south-carolina-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":62,\"name\":\"Vermont\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/vermont-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":63,\"name\":\"Employee Cost Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/employee-cost-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":64,\"name\":\"West Virginia\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/west-virginia-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":65,\"name\":\"New York City\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/new-york-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":66,\"name\":\"Los Angeles\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/los-angeles-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":67,\"name\":\"Chicago\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/chicago-tax-calculator\"}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com#author\",\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director, CPA\",\"description\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\",\"knowsAbout\":[\"Federal Income Tax\",\"State Income Tax\",\"FICA Tax\",\"Payroll Tax\",\"IRS Compliance\",\"Tax Planning\",\"Multi-State Taxation\",\"Tax-Advantaged Accounts\"],\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachelmitchellcpa/\",\"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/\"],\"worksFor\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"image\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\"},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#faq\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I calculate my take-home pay from my salary?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Start with your gross salary, subtract federal income tax (using progressive brackets), FICA (7.65% for Social Security and Medicare), and state income tax. Pre-tax deductions like 401(k) and HSA lower your taxable income. Use TheTaxCalc paycheck calculator for instant results.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is FICA and how much does it take from my paycheck?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"FICA is the payroll tax funding Social Security (6.2%, capped at $184,500 for 2026) and Medicare (1.45%, no cap). That's 7.65% total from every paycheck. An extra 0.9% Medicare surcharge applies on earnings over $200,000.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which states have no income tax?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Nine states have no personal income tax: Alaska, Florida, Nevada, New Hampshire, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming. TheTaxCalc supports TX and FL paycheck calculators with property tax and cost-of-living analysis.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much is taken out of a $75,000 salary in taxes?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"A single filer making $75K pays roughly $7,670 federal tax (after the $16,100 standard deduction), $5,738 FICA, plus state tax. In Texas or Florida (0% state tax), you keep around $61,600. In Illinois (4.95%), closer to $58,000.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does contributing to a 401(k) reduce my taxes?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Every dollar in a traditional 401(k) drops your taxable income for federal and state tax (but not FICA). Contributing $10,000 on a $75K salary saves over $2,200 in federal tax at the 22% bracket. The 2026 limit is $24,500.\"}}]}]}</script><section id=\"main-content\" class=\"relative overflow-hidden py-16 sm:py-24 bg-mesh-hero\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><div class=\"text-center space-y-6\"><div class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-emerald-400\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-zap h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 14a1 1 0 0 1-.78-1.63l9.9-10.2a.5.5 0 0 1 .86.46l-1.92 6.02A1 1 0 0 0 13 10h7a1 1 0 0 1 .78 1.63l-9.9 10.2a.5.5 0 0 1-.86-.46l1.92-6.02A1 1 0 0 0 11 14z\"></path></svg>Updated for 2026 Tax Year</div><h1 class=\"text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl\">Free <span class=\"gradient-text\">Tax Calculators</span><br/>for 2026</h1><p class=\"speakable-summary mx-auto max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Ever look at your pay stub and think “wait, they took <em>how</em>much?” Yeah, us too. We built these calculators so you can see exactly where your money goes —<strong class=\"text-foreground\"> federal tax</strong>, FICA, and<strong class=\"text-foreground\"> state taxes</strong> all broken down line by line. No guesswork, no surprises.</p><div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-8 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Your Paycheck</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 px-8 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:bg-muted/30 transition-all\" href=\"/relocation-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg>Compare States</a></div><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-6 pt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-users h-4 w-4 text-emerald-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"></path><path d=\"M16 3.128a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.744\"></path><path d=\"M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87\"></path><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"7\" r=\"4\"></circle></svg>100% Free</span><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield h-4 w-4 text-emerald-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.9