":\"New Mexico\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/new-mexico-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":58,\"name\":\"North Dakota\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/north-dakota-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":59,\"name\":\"Oklahoma\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/oklahoma-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":60,\"name\":\"Rhode Island\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/rhode-island-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":61,\"name\":\"South Carolina\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/south-carolina-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":62,\"name\":\"Vermont\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/vermont-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":63,\"name\":\"Employee Cost Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/employee-cost-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":64,\"name\":\"West Virginia\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/west-virginia-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":65,\"name\":\"New York City\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/new-york-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":66,\"name\":\"Los Angeles\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/los-angeles-tax-calculator\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":67,\"name\":\"Chicago\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/chicago-tax-calculator\"}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com#author\",\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director, CPA\",\"description\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\",\"knowsAbout\":[\"Federal Income Tax\",\"State Income Tax\",\"FICA Tax\",\"Payroll Tax\",\"IRS Compliance\",\"Tax Planning\",\"Multi-State Taxation\",\"Tax-Advantaged Accounts\"],\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachelmitchellcpa/\",\"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/\"],\"worksFor\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"image\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\"},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#faq\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I calculate my take-home pay from my salary?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Start with your gross salary, subtract federal income tax (using progressive brackets), FICA (7.65% for Social Security and Medicare), and state income tax. Pre-tax deductions like 401(k) and HSA lower your taxable income. Use TheTaxCalc paycheck calculator for instant results.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is FICA and how much does it take from my paycheck?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"FICA is the payroll tax funding Social Security (6.2%, capped at $184,500 for 2026) and Medicare (1.45%, no cap). That's 7.65% total from every paycheck. An extra 0.9% Medicare surcharge applies on earnings over $200,000.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which states have no income tax?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Nine states have no personal income tax: Alaska, Florida, Nevada, New Hampshire, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming. TheTaxCalc supports TX and FL paycheck calculators with property tax and cost-of-living analysis.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much is taken out of a $75,000 salary in taxes?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"A single filer making $75K pays roughly $7,670 federal tax (after the $16,100 standard deduction), $5,738 FICA, plus state tax. In Texas or Florida (0% state tax), you keep around $61,600. In Illinois (4.95%), closer to $58,000.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does contributing to a 401(k) reduce my taxes?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Every dollar in a traditional 401(k) drops your taxable income for federal and state tax (but not FICA). Contributing $10,000 on a $75K salary saves over $2,200 in federal tax at the 22% bracket. The 2026 limit is $24,500.\"}}]}]}5:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$1f\"}}],\"$L20\",\"$L21\",\"$L22\",\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\"],null,\"$L2a\"]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2b\",null,{\"children\":\"$L2c\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$2e\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$L2f\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\",\"content\":\"\"}]]}]\n8:[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/233p45nuh4m5b.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n9:[\"$\",\"link\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0dwp-mo_n_jm0.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n30:I[46236,[\"/_next/static/chunks/2g3ofza521d-d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3mzfoc5k_0lxh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/1h498-er8bjws.js\"],\"DynamicProviders\"]\n89:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/05-c3ty_6dwfk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/44p37290qsddb.js\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n11:[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/texas-tax-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/texas-tax-calculato